# `npm run preview` output: iteration frames plus their sidecar. These are
# working artefacts of an authoring loop, not documentation assets — the
# committed screenshots are the ones under docs/, produced by `npm run
# capture`.
#
# ALLOW-LIST, NOT A PLAIN IGNORE, and that is not fussiness. The preview
# PAGE now lives at `preview/` (index.html + main.ts, source that must be
# committed) and the script writes its frames, sidecars and scratch probes
# into the same folder, because `--out` defaults to the page's own name.
# Ignoring `/preview/` wholesale would silently swallow the page; listing
# extensions would let the next kind of scratch file through. So: ignore
# everything under it and re-admit exactly the two files that are source.
/preview/*
!/preview/index.html
!/preview/main.ts

# Scratch git worktrees used to isolate concurrent agents. These are real
# repositories, so an unqualified `git add -A` commits one as a gitlink and
# the next clone gets a dangling submodule reference it cannot resolve.
.claude/worktrees/

# The measured kit, if someone has put one here for the road demo to draw
# as a reference layer. Derived measurement of a copyrighted game, living
# outside both repositories: never ours to commit, and the page does
# without it.
/kit.json

# Where the measured kits live on THIS machine. The kits are measurements
# of a commercial product and neither they nor their filenames belong in a
# public checkout; see tests/support/kits.ts. Absent for almost everyone,
# which is why every suite that needs one skips.
/road-kits.local.json
